# Drive the compositor's desktop: put the pointer on the terminal, then
# type a command at it.
#
# The axis range is QEMU's own 0..=32767 rather than guest pixels: the
# host cannot know what mode the guest chose. The middle of the screen is
# inside the terminal window, which the desktop lays out with a margin
# around it, so this is what gives the terminal the keyboard — focus
# follows the pointer and nothing else moves it.
abs 16384 16384

# `echo hello`, one key at a time, then Enter. The terminal echoes what
# it is typed and the shell prints what it produces, so a capture taken
# after this shows the command on one row and its output on the next.
key e
key c
key h
key o
key spc
key h
key e
key l
key l
key o
key ret
